# Generated ECC instincts (#84). The extension says YAML but the content is
# markdown, so Prettier's YAML parser throws rather than reporting a style
# problem -- "A block sequence may not be used as an implicit map key". It is
# committed on main, so the lefthook `format` step failed on every commit that
# staged it, which any merge from main does. Ignoring it unblocks that without
# rewriting a generated file nobody hand-maintains.
.claude/homunculus/instincts/inherited/*.yaml

# Supabase CLI scratch state. It is ignored by the CLI's own nested
# `supabase/.gitignore`, not the root one, so `includeIgnoreFile()` never sees
# it either -- which is why `eslint.config.js` states it explicitly as well.
# Without this entry the `prettier --check .` file count depends on whether
# `supabase start` has been run, and `bun run format` writes into the directory
# holding `start-secrets/.../env/docker.env`.
supabase/.temp/

# PLAN.md (#139 follow-up). Prettier is NON-IDEMPOTENT on this file: it adds
# four spaces to one deeply nested list block on every run and never converges
# -- measured at line 553, indentation 18 -> 26 -> 30 -> 34 across successive
# writes. Because the lefthook `format` step runs `prettier --write` on staged
# files, and the project workflow commits PLAN.md on every task tick, each
# commit buried a ~370-line whitespace diff in itself and indented the block
# further. `907b24e` is the instance that made it visible: a 3-line edit
# carrying 186 lines of churn under a `ci:` subject.
PLAN.md

# Agent tooling scratch, matching `.gitignore`. Prettier does not read
# `.gitignore`, so it needs stating twice: without this, `prettier --check .`
# reports 78 files where `git ls-files` reports 50, and the difference is
# whichever skill happened to run on this machine. `format:ratchet` counts
# tracked files and is unaffected either way; this is what makes the figure in
# `bun run lint` mean the same thing.
.superpowers/
.impeccable/
